  "notes": [
   "The catalog prints 'List A - Complete one combination from the following: 3-5'. Each combination is recorded as its own block in option_group 'List A'. The 3-5 unit total is not stored on any single block.",
   "ERTH 111H & ERTH 111L is printed as its own List A combination. It is recorded as an honors alternative inside the ERTH 111 & 111L block.",
   "Footnote 1 says ERTH 141/141L are the same as GEOG 101/101L. The catalog prints them as separate combinations, so they are kept as separate List A blocks.",
   "Cross-listed courses (ENVS/ERTH 115, 115L, 116; HIST/ENVS 112; ERTH 142/GEOG 105; ERTH/GEOG 152) are recorded as one entry, with the cross-listed code as an alternative.",
   "The closed list stores 'ERTH152' and 'GEOG152' without a space. They are matched to the catalog's ERTH/GEOG 152 and not flagged as catalog additions.",
   "List C has no printed course list. It is a single course from the Cal-GETC Area 3A list, which the page only links to, so the block holds no courses.",
   "Units for 'or' alternatives and List A/B courses are not printed beside each course and are left null. Range rows such as 'BIOL 100 4-5' record the printed range on the first course only.",
   "The 'Total Units 54.00-62.00' figure is the major total. The 60-unit statement is the generic associate degree requirement, so degree_total is null.",
   "The GE options are the SBCC General Education pattern or the Cal-GETC pattern. No GE units are printed.",
